1
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Fate of one. Future of all.

2
00:08:56,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald is a fantasy,
adventure film directed by David Yates.

3
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:30,000
Gellert Grindelwald has escaped imprisonment and has begun gathering followers
to his cause—elevating wizards above all non-magical beings.

4
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:58,000
The only one capable of putting a stop to him is the wizard he
once called his closest friend, Albus Dumbledore.

5
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:26,000
However, Dumbledore will need to seek help from the wizard who had thwarted Grindelwald once before, his
former student Newt Scamander, who agrees to help, unaware of the dangers that lie ahead.

6
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Lines are drawn as love and loyalty are tested, even among the truest
friends and family, in an increasingly divided wizarding world.

7
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:22,000
Newt Scamander, played by Eddie Redmayne.

8
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:50,000
Tina Goldstein, played by Katherine Waterston.

9
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:18,000
Jacob Kowalski, played by Dan Fogler.

10
00:44:40,000 --> 00:44:46,000
Queenie Goldstein, played by Alison Sudol.

11
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:14,000
Grindelwald, played by Johnny Depp.

12
00:53:36,000 --> 00:53:42,000
Albus Dumbledore, played by Jude Law.

13
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:10,000
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald is a 2018 fantasy
film directed by David Yates and written by J.

14
01:02:32,000 --> 01:02:38,000
The sequel to Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find Them (2016), it is the second instalment in the
Fantastic Beasts film series and the tenth overall in the Wizarding World franchise.

15
01:07:00,000 --> 01:07:06,000
It features an ensemble cast including Eddie Redmayne, Katherine Waterston, Dan Fogler, Alison Sudol, Ezra Miller,
Zoë Kravitz, Callum Turner, Claudia Kim, William Nadylam, Kevin Guthrie, Jude Law, and Johnny Depp.

16
01:11:28,000 --> 01:11:34,000
Set in 1927, it follows Newt Scamander and Albus Dumbledore as they attempt to take down the dark
wizard Gellert Grindelwald while facing new threats in a more divided wizarding world.

17
01:15:56,000 --> 01:16:02,000
A second Fantastic Beasts film was announced in October 2014, and Rowling
confirmed in July 2016 that she had completed the script.

18
01:20:24,000 --> 01:20:30,000
Depp was cast in November 2016, causing some controversy due to
domestic violence allegations made against him.

19
01:24:52,000 --> 01:24:58,000
Law signed on in April 2017.

20
01:29:20,000 --> 01:29:26,000
Principal photography began in July 2017 at Warner Bros.

21
01:33:48,000 --> 01:33:54,000
Studios, Leavesden, in England.

22
01:38:16,000 --> 01:38:22,000
Filming also took place in London, Switzerland, and
Paris, and wrapped in December 2017.

23
01:42:44,000 --> 01:42:50,000
Fantastic Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald premiered in Paris on 8 November 2018, and was released
theatrically in the United Kingdom and United States on 16 November 2018, by Warner Bros.

24
01:47:12,000 --> 01:47:18,000
It grossed $654.9 million worldwide, making it the
tenth highest-grossing film of 2018.

25
01:51:40,000 --> 01:51:46,000
It became the lowest-grossing instalment of the Wizarding World franchise upon release, which it remained
until the release of its sequel, Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets of Dumbledore, in 2022.

26
01:56:08,000 --> 01:56:14,000
It received generally mixed reviews from critics, as it was viewed to have been filled
with too many characters and "overburdened" with sequel-dependent details.

27
02:00:36,000 --> 02:00:42,000
At the 72nd British Academy Film Awards, the film was nominated for
Best Production Design and Best Special Visual Effects.

28
02:05:04,000 --> 02:05:10,000
The sequel, Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets of
Dumbledore, was released in April 2022.

29
02:09:32,000 --> 02:09:38,000
The film explores themes of witch, new york city,
paris, france, magic, school of witchcraft.
